# Overlay image registry — cp overlays.conf.example overlays.conf, then edit.
#
# One entry per line, `name:path`. Each names a directory holding an overlay
# Dockerfile (project-specific tooling built ON TOP of the base image — see the
# multiplai-container README, "Overlay images", for the Dockerfile contract).
# The path is absolute, ~-prefixed, or relative to WORKSPACE.
#
# container/build.sh — which ./setup.sh runs — builds every entry after the
# base image, tagged `claude-multiplai-<name>:local`. Unchanged entries are
# cache no-ops; a changed base or overlay Dockerfile rebuilds automatically.
#
# Launch with an overlay by setting IMAGE_NAME in a profile (docs/PROFILES.md):
#   env.myproject:  IMAGE_NAME="claude-multiplai-myproject:local"
#
# myproject:PROJECTS/myproject/claude-overlay
